---
import { FAQSection, RelatedArticles } from "../../components/article";
import ComparisonTable from "../../components/article/ComparisonTable.astro";
import ArticleLayout from "../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";

const title = "Wise vs PayPal vs Payoneer: Best for Remote Workers?";
const description =
  "Compare Wise, PayPal, and Payoneer for international payments. Fees, exchange rates, speed, and features to help freelancers choose the right platform.";
const authorSlug = "daniel-brooks";
const pubDate = new Date("2025-07-06");
const readingTime = 10;
const image = "/images/unsplash/photo-1563013544-824ae1b704d3-1200w.webp";
const imageAlt = "International payment platforms comparison";

const headings = [
  {
    depth: 2,
    slug: "quick-answer",
    text: "Quick Answer: Which Should You Use?",
  },
  { depth: 2, slug: "wise-overview", text: "Wise Overview" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "paypal-overview", text: "PayPal Overview" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "payoneer-overview", text: "Payoneer Overview" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "feature-comparison", text: "Feature Comparison" },
  {
    depth: 2,
    slug: "fee-comparison",
    text: "The Money Test (The Real Numbers)",
  },
  { depth: 2, slug: "speed-comparison", text: "Speed of Transfers" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "best-use-cases", text: "Best Use Cases" },
  { depth: 2, slug: "faq", text: "Frequently Asked Questions" },
];

// Fee Comparison Data
const feeComparisonColumns = [
  { key: "platform", label: "Platform" },
  { key: "receivingFee", label: "Receiving Fee" },
  { key: "conversionFee", label: "Conversion Fee" },
  { key: "totalCost", label: "Total Cost" },
  { key: "youReceive", label: "You Receive" },
];

const feeComparisonRows = [
  {
    platform: "<strong>Wise</strong>",
    receivingFee: "$0",
    conversionFee: "~$5 (0.5%)",
    totalCost: "<strong>~$5</strong>",
    youReceive: "<strong>~£790</strong>",
  },
  {
    platform: "<strong>Payoneer</strong>",
    receivingFee: "$0",
    conversionFee: "~$20 (2%)",
    totalCost: "~$22",
    youReceive: "~£778",
  },
  {
    platform: "<strong>PayPal</strong>",
    receivingFee: "$44 (4.4%)",
    conversionFee: "~$30 (3%)",
    totalCost: "~$74",
    youReceive: "~£737",
  },
];

// Currency Support Data
const currencySupportColumns = [
  { key: "feature", label: "Feature" },
  { key: "wise", label: "Wise" },
  { key: "paypal", label: "PayPal" },
  { key: "payoneer", label: "Payoneer" },
];

const currencySupportRows = [
  {
    feature: "Currencies Supported",
    wise: "50+",
    paypal: "25+",
    payoneer: "150+",
  },
  {
    feature: "Multi-Currency Balance",
    wise: "Yes (50+)",
    paypal: "Limited",
    payoneer: "Yes (8)",
  },
  {
    feature: "Local Bank Details",
    wise: "10+ countries",
    paypal: "No",
    payoneer: "4+ countries",
  },
  {
    feature: "Exchange Rate Quality",
    wise: "Excellent",
    paypal: "Poor",
    payoneer: "Good",
  },
];

// Speed Comparison Data
const speedComparisonColumns = [
  { key: "platform", label: "Platform" },
  { key: "paymentToAccount", label: "Payment to Account" },
  { key: "withdrawalToBank", label: "Withdrawal to Bank" },
];

const speedComparisonRows = [
  {
    platform: "<strong>PayPal</strong>",
    paymentToAccount: "Instant",
    withdrawalToBank: "3-5 days (standard) / instant for 1%",
  },
  {
    platform: "<strong>Wise</strong>",
    paymentToAccount: "1-2 days",
    withdrawalToBank: "Same day to 2 days",
  },
  {
    platform: "<strong>Payoneer</strong>",
    paymentToAccount: "1-3 days",
    withdrawalToBank: "2-5 days",
  },
];

const faqData = [
  {
    question: "Which platform has the lowest fees overall?",
    answer: "Wise. Almost always. The 0.35-1% fee is unbeatable compared to PayPal's 4-6%.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can I use multiple platforms at once?",
    answer:
      "Yes. I do. Wise is my main. PayPal is for clients who refuse anything else. Payoneer is for my Upwork gigs.",
  },
  {
    question: "Which is safest for large payments?",
    answer:
      "They're all safe. Regulated. But PayPal likes to freeze accounts more than the others. For huge amounts ($10k+), I'd stick to Wise or a traditional bank wire.",
  },
  {
    question: "Which works best with freelance platforms like Upwork?",
    answer: "Payoneer. It's built into the dashboard of almost every gig site.",
  },
  {
    question: "Can I hold multiple currencies in these accounts?",
    answer:
      "Wise is best for this. 50+ currencies. You can hold Thai Baht, Euros, and Dollars all at once. PayPal lets you do it but charges you to convert.",
  },
  {
    question: "Which has the best mobile app?",
    answer: "PayPal's app is slick. Wise is clean and simple. Payoneer is... fine. It works.",
  },
];

const relatedArticles = [
  {
    title: "How to Accept International Payments",
    excerpt: "Complete guide to getting paid by international clients.",
    href: "/tools/accept-international-payments-freelancer",
    image: "/images/unsplash/photo-1526304640581-d334cdbbf45e-800w.webp",
    imageAlt: "International currency and payments",
  },
  {
    title: "Best Banking for Digital Nomads",
    excerpt: "Compare banking options for remote workers.",
    href: "/blog/best-banking-digital-nomads",
    image: "/images/unsplash/photo-1601597111158-2fceff292cdc-800w.webp",
    imageAlt: "Digital banking on mobile device",
  },
  {
    title: "Crypto-Friendly Banks",
    excerpt: "Banks that work with cryptocurrency for digital nomads.",
    href: "/blog/crypto-friendly-banks",
    image: "/images/unsplash/photo-1518546305927-5a555bb7020d-800w.webp",
    imageAlt: "Cryptocurrency and banking",
  },
];
---

<ArticleLayout
    title={title}
    description={description}
    authorSlug={authorSlug}
    pubDate={pubDate}
    readingTime={readingTime}
    image={image}
    imageAlt={imageAlt}
    category="Finance"
    categorySlug="tools/finance"
    headings={headings}
>
  <p class="lead">
    So there I was, staring at a $2,000 payment from a client. It landed in
    my PayPal account. Cool, right?
  </p>

  <p>Then I tried to withdraw it.</p>
  <p>Fee: $88.<br/>Exchange rate markup: Another $60 gone.</p>
  <p>
    I basically paid for a fancy dinner just to touch my own money. That was
    the last time I used PayPal as my default.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you're <a href="/guides/productivity">working remotely</a>, you're dealing with Wise, PayPal, or
    Payoneer. They look the same. They aren't.
  </p>
  <p>One is a dinosaur. One is a necessary evil. One is actually good.</p>

  <h2 id="quick-answer">Quick Answer: Which Should You Use?</h2>
  <p>You want the short version?</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Wise:</strong> Use this. Seriously. It's what I use for 90% of
      my stuff. Best rates, lowest fees.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>PayPal:</strong> Keep it because clients ask for it. But try
      not to use it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payoneer:</strong> Good if you're on <a href="/tools/best-online-course-platforms">freelance platforms</a>
      like Upwork or Fiverr. They integrate
      well.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    My setup? I have all three. Wise is the daily driver. PayPal is the
    backup. Payoneer is for platform work.
  </p>

  <h2 id="wise-overview">Wise Overview</h2>
  <p>This is the one I actually like.</p>
  <p>
    It used to be called TransferWise. It's basically a bank account that
    doesn't hate you.
  </p>

  <h3>Why it's good:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Real exchange rates.</strong> Google "USD to GBP" - that's the
      rate you get.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fees are transparent.</strong> They tell you "This costs $4.50"
      instead of hiding it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>You get local bank details.</strong> I have a US account number,
      a UK sort code, and an EU IBAN. All in one app.
    </li>
    <li><strong>The card works everywhere.</strong></li>
  </ul>

  <h3>The bad stuff:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No buyer protection.</strong> If you send money to a scammer,
      it's gone.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>It's not "instant" instant.</strong> Takes a day or two usually.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Some old-school clients have never heard of it.</strong>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="paypal-overview">PayPal Overview</h2>
  <p>The dinosaur.</p>
  <p>Everyone has it. That's the only reason it's still here.</p>

  <h3>The good:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Instant.</strong> Money is there right now.</li>
    <li>
      <strong><a href="/tools/accept-international-payments-freelancer">Clients</a> trust it.</strong> "Can I pay via
      PayPal?" is the most
      common email I get.
    </li>
    <li><strong>It's easy.</strong> Email address and done.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>The ugly:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The fees are insulting.</strong> 4% to receive? Plus a bad exchange
      rate? Come on.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>They freeze accounts.</strong> I know people who had $5k locked
      for 6 months because PayPal "suspected unusual activity."
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The exchange rate is a hidden tax.</strong> They say "no fee"
      then give you a rate 3% worse than the market.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="payoneer-overview">Payoneer Overview</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/guides/freelancer-tax-deductions-guide">freelancer</a> specialist.</p>
  <p>If you live on Upwork or Fiverr, you probably need this.</p>

  <h3>The vibe:</h3>
  <p>
    It's corporate but functional. Better fees than PayPal, worse than Wise.
  </p>

  <h3>Why use it:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Integrates with everything.</strong> Upwork, Amazon, Airbnb.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>You can get a Mastercard to spend your balance.</strong>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Good for mass payments if you're hiring people.</strong>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="feature-comparison">Feature Comparison</h2>
  <ComparisonTable
      columns={currencySupportColumns}
      rows={currencySupportRows}
  />

  <h2 id="fee-comparison">The Money Test (The Real Numbers)</h2>
  <p>
    Let's say a client sends you $1,000. You want it in your UK bank account
    (GBP).
  </p>

  <ComparisonTable
      columns={feeComparisonColumns}
      rows={feeComparisonRows}
      highlight={0}
  />

  <p>Look at that difference. £53.</p>
  <p>That's not "fees." That's a grocery run. That's a night out.</p>
  <p>
    Do that every month and you're losing £600 a year to PayPal. For what?
    Convenience?
  </p>

  <h2 id="speed-comparison">Speed of Transfers</h2>
  <ComparisonTable
      columns={speedComparisonColumns}
      rows={speedComparisonRows}
  />
  <p>PayPal wins on instant availability.</p>
  <p>Wise takes a day.</p>
  <p>Payoneer takes a few days.</p>
  <p>Is instant access worth $70? Not to me. I can wait 24 hours.</p>

  <h2 id="best-use-cases">Best Use Cases</h2>

  <h3>Use Wise When:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>You want to keep your money.</li>
    <li>You have <a href="/tools/best-invoicing-tools">regular clients</a> who can pay via bank transfer.</li>
    <li>You <a href="/blog/top-destinations-digital-nomads">travel</a>. The card is a lifesaver.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Use PayPal When:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The client refuses everything else.</li>
    <li>It's a small amount ($50) and you don't care about the fee.</li>
    <li>You need buyer protection for a purchase.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Use Payoneer When:</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Your platform (Upwork/Fiverr) forces you to.</li>
    <li>You need a physical card but can't get Wise.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <FAQSection faqs={faqData}/>

  <h2>Final Verdict</h2>
  <p>Get Wise. Use it for everything you can.</p>
  <p>
    The exchange rates alone justify it. Stop donating 4% of your income to
    PayPal. You worked for that money. Keep it.
  </p>
  <p>
    But keep a PayPal account open. You'll need it eventually. Just don't
    let it be your default.
  </p>

  <Fragment slot="full-width">
    <RelatedArticles articles={relatedArticles}/>
  </Fragment>
</ArticleLayout>
